---
alwaysApply: false
description: n8n rules when creating or calling N8N workflows
---
For user actions that trigger an n8n workflow, implement the following:
Create an n8n workflow with “Header” authorization. Never create a public n8n workflow (i.e., with None as authorization). Choose the header named “Header Auth X-Webhook-Secret”. Never overwrite its value.

The frontend should call an edge function. Do not call n8n directly from the frontend. Why? Because a secret is required and must not be exposed client-side.
Inside the edge function, call n8n using the snippet below (where `WEBHOOK_URL` is your actual n8n webhook URL; it can be hardcoded in the edge function). Refer to `supabase/functions/feedback-upload` for a full example.
    const forwardHeaders: Record<string, string> = { "Content-Type": "application/json" };

    const WEBHOOK_SECRET = Deno.env.get("N8N_X_WEBHOOK_SECRET");


    forwardHeaders["X-Webhook-Secret"] = WEBHOOK_SECRET;


    const forwardBody = {
      ...
    };

    const forwardRes = await fetch(WEBHOOK_URL, {
      method: "POST",
      headers: forwardHeaders,
      body: JSON.stringify(forwardBody),
    });

      headers: forwardHeaders,
      body: JSON.stringify(forwardBody),
    });
